    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet in one of Foxrock's most sought-after residential addresses, this impressive five-bedroom, five-bathroom detached home combines generous proportions, timeless appeal and excellent family accommodation. Brick-fronted and set amid extensive private grounds, the property enjoys a wonderful sense of space and privacy, complemented by a large, detached garage, electric gates and mature gardens. The substantial accommodation, together with a converted attic, offers exceptional flexibility for modern family living, while its position in the heart of Foxrock places it within easy reach of a wealth of established amenities.\n\nThe accommodation is thoughtfully arranged over two floors, with the welcoming entrance hallway opening into the drawing room, dining room and study. The generous kitchen to the left of the hallway further enhances the ground-floor layout, with a large dining area and double doors into the inner hallway, off which is a guest w.c., utility room and separate living room. A further guest w.c. is located off the entrance hall. Upstairs, five well-proportioned bedrooms include excellent accommodation for a large family, with the principal bedroom enjoying a walk-in wardrobe and en-suite, while bedroom three also benefits from an en-suite. The family bathroom completes the accommodation at this level. The converted attic adds a valuable further space, ideal as a home office, playroom, studio or additional living area. Externally, there is a gravel driveway with off street parking for multiple cars, and large lawn areas set behind electric gates. A double garage to the left also add ancillary accommodation and could be used as a gym, workshop or garage for cars.\n\nFoxrock is renowned for its leafy residential setting, excellent schools and strong community atmosphere, while offering convenient access to Dublin city and the surrounding suburbs. A selection of schools are close by, including Loreto College Foxrock, St Brigid's Boys' National School and Lycée Français Samuel Beckett Primary School. The village provides a choice of cafés, restaurants, specialist shops and everyday services, with further retail and leisure facilities available at nearby Cornelscourt, Stillorgan and Dundrum. The area is also well serviced by public transport, with bus services connecting Foxrock with surrounding suburbs and the city, while the Luas Green Line is accessible at nearby stations including Carrickmines, providing a direct connection towards Dublin city centre and beyond."
      },
